QUICraft patch for Netty netty-4.2.19.Final (commit 64cc10f38ea5f5bd7eae48507817c66680d0afdc):
complete a client connect in the same round trip as the handshake.

Netty's certificate verifier returns ssl_verify_retry and runs the verification as an SSL task
after quiche_conn_recv. quiche resumes the paused handshake only when it is next driven, and that
is the connectionSend(...) in recvComplete(), because quiche's send() calls do_handshake. That
send writes the client Finished and the connection is now established. Nothing checked for it
until the server's next packet arrived, so the connect future completed one RTT late (~2 RTT in
total instead of ~1).

Fix: after each connectionSend(...) that can follow an SSL task (recvComplete() and the three
event-loop continuations after SSL tasks), a client whose connect promise is still pending and
whose connection is now established runs processReceived(...) (channelActive, connect promise)
and sends again, so whatever the listeners wrote goes out at once.

Applied by natives/build-netty-quic.sh with `git apply`, which ignores this text.

